ESP32 ELECTRONIC DRUM - CONNECTIONS
===================================

PROJECT COMPONENTS
------------------
1. ESP32 Development Board
2. Piezo Sensor 1
3. Piezo Sensor 2
4. DFPlayer Mini
5. Speaker
6. Green LED
7. Red LED
8. 220-330 ohm resistors for LEDs
9. 10k ohm resistors for piezo inputs
10. 1M ohm resistors for piezo pull-down
11. 1k ohm resistor for DFPlayer RX line


ESP32 PIN ASSIGNMENT
--------------------

Piezo Sensor 1:
Piezo positive  -> 10k resistor -> GPIO 34
Piezo negative  -> GND
GPIO 34         -> 1M resistor -> GND

Function:
Piezo 1 triggers Track 1 and Green LED.


Piezo Sensor 2:
Piezo positive  -> 10k resistor -> GPIO 35
Piezo negative  -> GND
GPIO 35         -> 1M resistor -> GND

Function:
Piezo 2 triggers Track 2 and Red LED.


GREEN LED
---------
ESP32 GPIO 25 -> 220-330 ohm resistor -> Green LED positive (+)
Green LED negative (-) -> GND

Function:
Flashes when Piezo Sensor 1 is hit.


RED LED
-------
ESP32 GPIO 26 -> 220-330 ohm resistor -> Red LED positive (+)
Red LED negative (-) -> GND

Function:
Flashes when Piezo Sensor 2 is hit.


DFPLAYER MINI
-------------
DFPlayer VCC -> ESP32 5V / VIN
DFPlayer GND -> ESP32 GND

DFPlayer TX  -> ESP32 GPIO 16

ESP32 GPIO 17
      |
      1k ohm resistor
      |
DFPlayer RX

Important:
ESP32 and DFPlayer must share the same GND.


SPEAKER
-------
Speaker wire 1 -> DFPlayer SPK1
Speaker wire 2 -> DFPlayer SPK2

Use SPK1 and SPK2 for a small passive speaker.

Do not connect the speaker directly to the ESP32.


